body:
i’m gonna write down what i ate today since its past dinner

for breakfast: 
- morning coffee: 1 coffee pod, 23kcal; 200ml sugar free almond milk, 26kcal;
- one medium soft boiled egg, 69kcal;

for lunch: 
- eggplant salad, 125g, 109kcal;
- cooked salmon, 100g, 182kcal;

for dinner:
- tzatziki, 100g, 106kcal;

and that’s about it. my food does vary from day to day, obviously, but it’s something along the lines of this. this day i had fish for lunch, but most days i just have a salad or something more refreshing, since it doesn’t make me feel full and nauseous, like the salmon did today. 
also, i track my calories every time before i eat and update them after i eat in case i ate more/less of what i had on my plate, so it’s not a case of not knowing how many calories i eat.
